course: dictionary
lesson: 5760
title: Lucky and luck
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lucky means good things happen by chance, not because of what you did. «You're so lucky, you don't have to do anything» shows this: the cousin did not earn the easy life, it just came to them.
explain: The second meaning is about charms and numbers. «A lucky number» is one people think will bring good luck. A lucky charm is an object people carry for the same reason.
explain: Maths gives you a check. A coin has an equal chance of heads or tails, and a lucky number does not win more often. Swap your meaning into the sentence: if lucky means "by chance", does the sentence still make sense?
fact: Lucky means having good things happen by chance, not because of what you did.
fact: Lucky can also mean bringing good luck, as in «a lucky number».
fact: A lucky charm is an object that people believe brings good luck.
fact: A lucky number does not win more often; each pack or box has the same chance.
fact: Lucky, luckier and luckiest show how much luck someone has.
exercise: «You're so lucky, you don't have to do anything.» What does lucky mean here? | Working very hard every day | Being good at maths | Feeling unwell | *Having good things happen by chance
exercise: Nadia says a lucky number wins more often. What is the best answer? | It wins only on Sundays | It makes you taller | Yes, it always wins | *No, a lucky number has the same chance as any other
exercise: What does «a lucky escape» mean? | Running away on purpose | Planning a long trip | *Escaping danger through good chance | Paying for a ticket to leave
test: «In 1414 a giraffe was painted because people thought it was a lucky mythical beast.» Lucky here means: | Having good things happen by chance | Hungry | *Bringing good luck | Very tall
test: Grace says her pencil is lucky because it works. Why might she be wrong? | Pencils are never lucky | Grace has bad eyesight | *She remembers the times it worked and forgets the misses | Pencils only work on Fridays
exam: Jayden says a lucky charm always brings good luck. What is the best answer? | It depends on the colour | Yes, it always works | Only on Tuesdays | *No, luck is chance, so a charm cannot make a good result certain
